WEBVTT

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:07.860
You mustn't call us cute!
kawaii nante sonna koto ittcha dame desu

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:21.910
Fluffy and lighthearted
fuwa fuwa

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:26.170
The strawberry girls are coming
ichigotachi ga yattekuru

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:30.510
Loud voices are coming closer
urusai koe ga chikazuite kuru

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:33.800
Fluffy and lighthearted
fuwa fuwa

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:37.970
The strawberry girls are coming
ichigo tachi ga yattekuru

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:42.520
They smell sweet and sour
amakute suppai kaori ga suru

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:46.770
It doesn't matter if the colors are mixed up
chiguhagu na iro de iimon

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:49.520
Let's draw some graffiti
rakugaki shichao

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:52.860
It's only natural that we'll make mistakes
shippai mo atarimae dayone

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:57.280
So you'd better forgive us!
watashitachi wo yurushite agenasai!

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:02.000
Don't get mad, don't get mad
okoranaidene, okoranaide

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.790
Just let us do what we want
suki ni sasete ne

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:07.500
Adults can't understand this
otona niwa wakaranai

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.800
Amazing! Miracle! Perfect!
suteki! kiseki! kanpeki!

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:16.590
You mustn't say we're cute!
kawaii nante sonna koto ittcha dame desu

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:20.260
Dazzling smiles
totetsumonai egao

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:22.720
Marshmallow-y sweet girls!
mashimaro na onnanoko

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:25.480
S-T-R-A-W-B-E-R-R-Y Girl!
I-C-H-I-G-O Girl!

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:28.480
Go, go, girl! "Strawberry" LOVE
Go, go, girl! "Ichigo" LOVE!

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:39.700
Mama's miso soup is the best!

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:42.790
Her clam miso soup is especially good!

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:45.120
Mama, please pass the soy sauce?

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:47.370
Natto is best with soy sauce.

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:49.540
Of course, here's the soy sauce, dear.

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:51.040
Oh, thanks!

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:52.880
And could I have a little mustard, too?

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:55.970
Oh, papa, I think it's better with kimchi!

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:58.550
Never mind the kimchi. Listen carefully...

00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:01.680
You must settle into your new school quickly.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:04.970
Yes, remember your behavior as a lady...

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:08.480
Oh... I just spilled the natto on my shirt.

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:12.520
Papa, you have to stir the natto really well...

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:16.190
...and then in one motion you pour it on your rice... like this.

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:17.900
I see.

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:21.070
As your father, I cannot help admiring how you cut the natto threads...

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:23.700
...with your skillful manipulation of the chopsticks.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:26.120
That's how a lady is.

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:28.330
You're right.

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:40.010
I'm off to school now!

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:55.530
It's finally arrived.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:58.700
The day of my debut at my new school.

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:12.290
Ana

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:16.300
It's been 5 years since we moved from England because of Papa's job.

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:19.470
I've gotten pretty used to the way of life here.

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:21.300
I'm even fluent in Japanese.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.340
And I love miso soup, too.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:26.430
From being here this long,
I've become quite attached to Japan.

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:27.890
<b>School Zone
From being here this long,
I've become quite attached to Japan.</b>

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:34.310
But, I...

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:43.240
I was so desperate that time.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:48.580
In Japan, everyone shies away from me when they see my hair and eyes.

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:53.790
I have to give people a good impression of my friendly personality right away.

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:56.130
I have to hook them right away.

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:58.170
A good hook is vital, Ana!

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:02.800
Everyone, nice to meet you!

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:06.100
I was born in England, in a wall of corn.

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:12.020
Oh, silly me, not a wall of corn...

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:13.770
I was born in Cornwall.

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:17.610
Cornwall.

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:19.820
Corn...

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:30.120
The past is the past!
The future is the future!

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:32.120
I won't make the same mistake twice!

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:38.960
Anyway, why does an English girl like me have to speak Japanese?

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:43.130
Besides, isn't Japanese kind of uncool?

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:46.300
All Papa and Mama speak now is Japanese...

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:50.060
...so I've almost completely forgotten English.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:52.100
But, I'm English.

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:54.810
I want to stay English.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:58.440
Hey, it's a foreigner.

00:04:58.440 --> 00:04:59.730
Yeah, it is.

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:03.740
Since it's my first day of school, nobody knows the truth about me.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:10.370
Nobody knows that I'm fluent in Japanese or that I like clam miso soup!

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:12.950
From today, I won't speak one bit of Japanese!

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:15.160
From today I will say good-bye to Japanese!

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:18.250
From today I will be English!

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:19.880
Good morning!

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:25.300
Oh, good day!

00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:34.600
She fell down after I greeted her.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:37.440
You sure have courage, to approach strangers like that.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:38.980
You know she's a foreigner, right?

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:41.440
But, she was talking in Japanese.

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:42.690
Was she really?

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:48.200
That's right, even though it's morning she said, "good day."

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:51.740
E-Excuse me, but...

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:55.250
In what grade might you two be?

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:56.870
Sixth grade, class 2.

00:05:57.370 --> 00:05:58.420
Thank goodness...

00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:01.130
If they're in a different grade,
I'm still safe.

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:03.550
You want a piece of this?

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:07.590
Just because she's cute, she thinks she can mouth off to us, boss!

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:09.140
Who are you calling boss?!

00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:10.140
Get 'er!

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:11.890
I'm not an underling, either!

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:14.390
Hey, you're just gonna leave us here?

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:17.640
Help me!

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:19.980
I don't get it, Micchan.

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:26.400
All right, I think that's gonna be my gimmick today.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:27.820
Is that so.

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:32.370
I slipped up immediately this morning...

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:34.370
But, now for the real test.

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:54.060
Okay, everyone, quiet!

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:57.100
I'm going to introduce a new student today.

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:01.810
Um... Introduce yourself.

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:03.480
Name.

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:05.980
Um...

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:09.490
"Your name, please, on the...
...on the blackboard."

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:10.450
Yes.

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:13.530
It's English. It's English.

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:14.990
Um...

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:20.960
A... na...

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:29.590
My name is Ana.

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:32.050
I came from England.

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:33.800
How do you do?

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:36.220
Nice to meet you!

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:41.230
<i>Whoa, I can totally understand her.</i>

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:43.600
<i>Maybe I do have a knack for English.</i>

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:46.230
<i>Does this girl really come from England?</i>

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:50.650
Excellent, they don't suspect a thing.

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:56.030
<i>Now, how do I say
"Glad to make your acquaintance"?</i>

00:07:57.740 --> 00:07:59.160
One, please?
Note: Literal translation of "hitotsu yoroshiku onegaishimasu"

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:04.330
Note: Literal translation of "hitotsu yoroshiku onegaishimasu"

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:06.040
Did everyone understand?

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:08.340
That means,
"Glad to make your acquaintance."

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:10.420
Sensei, doesn't that...

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:12.090
Go stand in the hallway, Sasazuka.

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:15.760
Regarding the seating...

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:19.560
I'd like everyone from this row to move back one.

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:23.690
She's going to sit in this front seat.

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:28.230
I'm sure there are lots of things she doesn't know yet...

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:31.320
...so I have to help her.

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:34.740
S-Sensei, excuse me, but...

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:50.590
Hello.

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:52.380
Hello...

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:01.180
Hello.

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:02.560
H-H-H... Hello.

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:09.690
I may have gone a little too far, but...

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:12.990
I think this girl is over-reacting a little.

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:29.210
Read from the 5th line.

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:31.960
I don't understand Japanese.

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:33.510
Then you may be seated.

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:34.760
I did it!

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:37.550
See, you understand.

00:09:40.930 --> 00:09:42.310
Why me?

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:47.560
Solve this equation.

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:50.110
I thought I told you
"I don't understand Japanese."

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:53.860
But this is math.

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:55.240
Uh-oh.

00:10:00.530 --> 00:10:03.540
Satake

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:06.290
This is an American joke.

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:07.250
I see.

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:11.040
Like I said... Why me?

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:25.980
DAILY CHORES
Miu Matsuoka
Keiko Yada

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:35.190
Micchan.

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:36.570
Uh-huh?

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:37.950
You know, right?

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:40.870
We're on daily chore duty, right?

00:10:40.870 --> 00:10:42.030
Oh, yeah!

00:10:42.030 --> 00:10:43.330
Then, take care of this.

00:10:43.870 --> 00:10:45.330
Oh my god!

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:47.750
This is discrimination.

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:50.370
I'm not even on daily chore duty!

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:52.500
I will fight against it surely.

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:54.250
But, it's your turn to be on daily chore duty.

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:58.510
Who's this Shirley?

00:10:58.510 --> 00:11:00.050
Probably nobody.

00:11:00.050 --> 00:11:00.800
Then where?

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:02.640
What do you mean, where?

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:05.060
Chi-chan, that's no good.

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:08.100
Even though you're young, you sure don't have much of an inquisitive mind.

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:09.520
What should I be inquisitive about?

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:14.690
So, what exactly are you inquiring about?

00:11:15.110 --> 00:11:16.530
Hey, look at this.

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:17.610
What is it?

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:18.030
I found a funny place name!

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:19.650
Eromanga Island
I found a funny place name!

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:26.370
Hey, don't you leave me, Chi-chan!

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:33.920
Um...

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:37.250
Hello.

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:39.090
Hello.

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:42.260
Um... Where in England did you come from?

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:43.800
C...

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:45.890
Oh no!

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:48.270
I was about to answer her automatically!

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:51.810
Now, how do you ask someone to repeat what they said?

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:55.060
"Why"? That's not it.

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:57.360
"How"? That's wrong too!

00:11:57.780 --> 00:11:58.690
I know!

00:11:59.690 --> 00:12:00.610
What?

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:05.120
D-Did I get it wrong?

00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:08.580
Um, Ana-chan...

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:10.580
Where... did... you... come... from?

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:12.040
Okay!

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:24.840
Yeah, you're right. This is Japan.

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:29.390
<i>By the side of the courtyard...</i>

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:31.520
That was close.

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:36.520
I was saved only because she thought I couldn't understand Japanese.

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:40.190
I can't let my guard down.

00:12:41.110 --> 00:12:42.780
Who knows the meaning of these?

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:44.150
I do.

00:12:44.150 --> 00:12:45.780
Are you boasting, Sasazuka?

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:48.530
"Simplicity and fortitude" means...

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:51.410
Who knows how to read this?

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:55.330
Don't let your guard down.

00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:58.630
Sasazuka, if you don't know, go stand in the hall.

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:03.970
Who knows what happens next?

00:13:04.170 --> 00:13:06.930
Don't let your guard down.

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:11.810
Thank you for this meal!

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:19.980
Oh no.

00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:23.240
I almost doomed myself!

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:25.950
She crossed her hands.
She rejected the school lunch!

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:27.820
This must be what they call a cultural clash!

00:13:27.820 --> 00:13:29.910
I guess the English probably prefer bread?

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:30.700
Of course!

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:32.950
They don't eat miso soup, but other soups!

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:34.120
It's no good.

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:37.170
It would be suspicious if an English person...

00:13:37.170 --> 00:13:38.460
...was able to use chopsticks skillfully.

00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:41.710
I somehow have to pretend
I don't know how to use them.

00:13:54.220 --> 00:13:56.520
I-It's so difficult.

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:18.420
Do you understand, Sasazuka?

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:20.710
This is the British style.

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:24.420
Anyhow, go stand in the hall.

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:34.850
This was a mistake...

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:36.810
If I don't speak Japanese...

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:40.100
...then I can't communicate with the people around me.

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:43.480
But I can't change directions this late on...

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:03.790
Huh?

00:15:05.090 --> 00:15:07.710
Just how weak are you?

00:15:08.130 --> 00:15:10.590
It opened easily!

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:11.840
Th-Thank...

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:23.270
I'm totally exposed.

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:30.900
Listen carefully!

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:35.280
I have no desire to speak Japanese at this school.

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:38.330
So, everything you heard just now...

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:39.460
H-Huh?

00:15:39.460 --> 00:15:40.250
What?

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:42.620
Ana-chan, you can speak Japanese?

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:53.300
Why are you asking me now?

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:54.890
Are you trying to deny it?

00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:57.060
Didn't you just hear me talking?

00:15:57.810 --> 00:15:59.850
You were staring at me!

00:15:59.850 --> 00:16:01.850
Please don't play dumb with me!

00:16:01.850 --> 00:16:08.400
Th-That was because...
you had rice... on your ch-cheek.

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:10.570
It was b-bothering me...

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:24.830
So, you didn't notice my speaking
Japanese a few moments ago?

00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:26.080
Huh?

00:16:26.080 --> 00:16:27.670
Don't "huh" at me!

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:31.670
Um... You were speaking Japanese?

00:16:59.240 --> 00:17:00.910
Oh, I see.

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:05.170
You decided not to speak Japanese, and that's why...

00:17:05.170 --> 00:17:08.290
Yes, I am English after all.

00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:12.420
But I don't think you can make friends if you only speak English...

00:17:16.050 --> 00:17:18.800
Oh, no, I'm sure that's not true.

00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:21.220
The barriers of language shouldn't matter.

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:23.930
Besides, you're good at Japanese.

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:27.100
You mustn't tell that to anyone!

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:29.150
Oh, that's right...

00:17:30.610 --> 00:17:32.320
Will you please keep it a secret?

00:17:34.530 --> 00:17:36.570
Yes.

00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:45.620
Oh yeah, Ana-chan...

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:49.500
I promised to walk home with my friends today.

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:51.000
Is that right?

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:53.340
Yes, I'm supposed to meet them here.

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:54.720
I don't mind.

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:57.300
But don't forget.

00:17:57.300 --> 00:18:00.430
I won't speak Japanese in front of anyone else but you.

00:18:00.430 --> 00:18:01.470
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:05.310
Oh, it's the foreigner from this morning who's fluent in Japanese.

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:07.890
I'm home!

00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:10.940
Oh, welcome home.

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:14.990
Hey, why are you home earlier than us?

00:18:14.990 --> 00:18:17.450
Would you like to know my secret?

00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:18.360
Not really.

00:18:18.360 --> 00:18:19.660
What?

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:24.040
More importantly, this girl joined Matsuri-chan's class today.

00:18:24.450 --> 00:18:25.950
She's called Ana-chan.

00:18:28.830 --> 00:18:30.290
Are you listening?

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:32.710
<b><i>Chika's Room</i></b>

00:18:32.710 --> 00:18:34.000
Onee-chan?
<b><i>Chika's Room</i></b>

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:36.920
Silky blonde hair.

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:42.640
Clear blue eyes.

00:18:43.390 --> 00:18:45.810
Skin as white as porcelain.

00:18:46.520 --> 00:18:49.980
Slender long legs...

00:18:54.190 --> 00:18:55.690
This one's mine!

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:57.900
Onee-chan's turned into a deranged person!

00:18:57.900 --> 00:18:59.820
There are a lot of empty cans!

00:18:59.820 --> 00:19:03.830
That's right, Nobue-oneechan gets even stupider when she drinks.

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:07.000
So, you're Ana-chan.

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:08.710
Sorry about that just now.

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:11.000
I'm terrible.

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:12.830
That's okay.

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:16.170
For goodness sake, how many did you drink all by yourself?

00:19:16.710 --> 00:19:17.460
Five!

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:18.880
Don't brag about it!

00:19:18.880 --> 00:19:22.300
All that drinking is why you tackled her!

00:19:22.680 --> 00:19:23.390
Right?

00:19:23.390 --> 00:19:25.720
I really don't mind.

00:19:26.010 --> 00:19:28.390
Well, she's so cute!

00:19:29.020 --> 00:19:30.270
Y-You're too kind...

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:34.440
She is cute, and she's so fluent in Japanese!

00:19:34.440 --> 00:19:36.610
Leave her alone already!

00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:40.740
But it's so amazing, given that she's English and all.

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:42.240
Oh yeah!

00:19:42.240 --> 00:19:45.910
Is it true that the English don't put lemon in their tea?

00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:49.290
Yes, they drink it plain or with milk.

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:54.250
It's always been a mystery to me, but do you put the milk or the tea in first?

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:58.920
If you mix hot tea and cold milk together it curdles and gets all clumpy...

00:19:59.670 --> 00:20:02.180
...so I've heard it's best to pour in the tea last.

00:20:03.590 --> 00:20:05.890
So... So... the curry flavor...

00:20:07.430 --> 00:20:08.720
Oh yeah, by the way...

00:20:09.310 --> 00:20:12.230
What's your surname, Ana-chan?

00:20:12.230 --> 00:20:17.190
Oh... Uh... It's not really worth sharing.

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:18.940
Huh? Why? Why?

00:20:18.940 --> 00:20:20.740
Please, never mind that.

00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:22.240
The truth is...

00:20:22.240 --> 00:20:25.200
...she's a samurai who hides her identity and wanders around saving the world.

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:27.030
You know that she's English.

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:30.160
Just call me Ana.

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:32.210
Come on and tell us!

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:33.830
Please, don't worry about it.

00:20:33.830 --> 00:20:36.130
It's not an important name.

00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:37.420
Onee-chan...

00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:37.920
Huh?

00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:39.590
What does this say?

00:20:41.510 --> 00:20:44.090
You ought to learn to read at least this much...

00:20:45.140 --> 00:20:46.760
Ana...

00:20:46.760 --> 00:20:48.350
...Coppola...

00:20:48.350 --> 00:20:49.140
Coppola.

00:20:49.510 --> 00:20:50.640
Coppola?

00:20:51.020 --> 00:20:52.060
Coppola.

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:53.940
Coppola.

00:21:03.610 --> 00:21:05.610
<i>Kind of weird...</i>

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:17.540
Don't worry about it!

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:20.750
It's a great name! Coppola!
Coppola-chan!

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:22.380
Quit repeating it!

00:21:25.510 --> 00:21:31.100
I know, let's all come up with a new nickname for Coppola-chan!

00:21:32.310 --> 00:21:33.140
Hey, hey.

00:21:34.020 --> 00:21:36.060
Ana-chan is depressed now.

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:41.440
In that case!

00:21:41.780 --> 00:21:43.400
This will fix everything!

00:21:46.110 --> 00:21:47.410
Look, look!

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:51.620
<b>New Name</b>

00:21:53.950 --> 00:21:56.830
Why me?

00:21:56.830 --> 00:22:08.090
<i>~ Bamboo laundry poles for sale ~</i>

00:22:15.640 --> 00:22:26.030
When I remembered my forgotten dream
wasurekaketa yume wo omoidashitara

00:22:27.110 --> 00:22:37.290
Suddenly your smile came to mind
fui ni kimi no egao ga ukandekitayo

00:22:37.790 --> 00:22:43.840
Without even thinking about tomorrow
ashita sae mada shiranai

00:22:43.840 --> 00:22:49.260
We used to play all day
nee asonde bakari ita ano hi

00:22:50.010 --> 00:22:55.180
Even when there was a steep downhill
kyuuna sakamichi demo

00:22:55.180 --> 00:23:03.400
We ran as we pretended to have no fear
nee heiki na furi shite hashitta

00:23:03.860 --> 00:23:07.030
Hurry! Hurry!
isoide isoide

00:23:07.030 --> 00:23:14.740
A naughty shadow whispers in your ear
mimimoto de sasayaku itazura kageboshi

00:23:15.120 --> 00:23:18.410
Our skirts fluttered
sukaato yurameki

00:23:18.410 --> 00:23:23.460
As a cool breeze tapped our knees
suzukaze ga hiza wo tataita

00:23:23.840 --> 00:23:34.680
Where are you right now?
anone kimi wa ima doko ni imasuka?

00:23:41.100 --> 00:23:42.480
Meow!

00:23:42.480 --> 00:23:43.980
Oh, Matsuri-chan!

00:23:43.980 --> 00:23:45.690
Matsuri-chan turned into a cat!

00:23:45.690 --> 00:23:46.480
What?

00:23:46.480 --> 00:23:47.980
Look! There are her ears.

00:23:47.980 --> 00:23:49.110
Her tail.

00:23:49.110 --> 00:23:50.570
She's even wearing a bell!

00:23:51.910 --> 00:23:52.700
Ouch!

00:23:52.700 --> 00:23:56.450
Matsuri-chan, don't scratch me with your claws out!

00:23:56.450 --> 00:23:58.120
Hello, nya!

00:23:58.120 --> 00:24:00.870
There are two of Matsuri-chan?

00:24:01.210 --> 00:24:01.790
Huh?

00:24:01.790 --> 00:24:02.710
Just leave her alone.

00:24:02.710 --> 00:24:04.460
Let's go to Ana-chan's house.

00:24:05.040 --> 00:24:07.750
Watch the next "Marshmallow"!
House Call
Next

00:24:07.750 --> 00:24:10.010
